calculations, start with `table = pd.DataFrame(...)`, replacing `...` with the input argument. Calculate from the input passed to your function, not from the global CSV variable. Hidden checks use different numbers with the same columns and rules.\"]}, {\"cell_type\": \"code\", \"metadata\": {}, \"source\": [\"def regression_errors(actual, predicted):\\n\", \"    # Replace this placeholder with your solution.\\n\", \"    raise NotImplementedError(\\\"Complete this task\\\")\\n\"], \"execution_count\": null, \"outputs\": []}, {\"cell_type\": \"markdown\", \"metadata\": {}, \"source\": [\"## Structured interpretation — 30 marks\\n\", \"Choose exactly one option per question. Each is worth 5 marks. These questions use the stated scenarios; do not replace their supplied values with your CSV results.\\n\", \"\\n\", \"**D1. Why keep all records for an equipment ID in one partition?**\\n\", \"\\n\", \"A: To make all partition sizes equal. | B: To select equipment using target values. | C: To avoid evaluating on equipment already represented during fitting.\\n\", \"\\n\", \"**D2. Which records may determine the median used to fill missing model inputs?**\\n\", \"\\n\", \"A: Training records only; reuse those medians for validation and test. | B: All records before splitting. | C: Test records because they are the newest.\\n\", \"\\n\", \"**D3. Supplied validation MAE: baseline 4.0, linear 1.2, tree 1.8 target units. Select by smallest validation MAE.**\\n\", \"\\n\", \"A: Baseline. | B: Linear. | C: Tree.\\n\", \"\\n\", \"**D4. When may E6 test targets be used?**\\n\", \"\\n\", \"A: While choosing the model with the smallest error. | B: To fit the imputer. | C: Once for final evaluation after model selection is fixed.\\n\", \"\\n\", \"**D5. A few predictions have very large errors. Why can RMSE exceed MAE?**\\n\", \"\\n\", \"A: Squaring errors gives larger errors more influence. | B: RMSE is a percentage. | C: MAE ignores every large error.\\n\", \"\\n\", \"**D6. A model performs well on this synthetic dataset. What is the next justified step?**\\n\", \"\\n\", \"A: Deploy it as a safety system immediately. | B: Evaluate representative measured data and operating conditions before considering deployment. | C: Claim it works on every engineering system.\"]}, {\"cell_type\": \"code\", \"metadata\": {}, \"source\": [\"DECISIONS = {\\\"D1\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"D2\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"D3\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"D4\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"D5\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"D6\\\": \\\"\\\"}\\n\"], \"execution_count\": null, \"outputs\": []}, {\"cell_type\": \"markdown\", \"metadata\": {}, \"source\": [\"## Run your functions on the supplied CSV\\n\", \"Run this supplied cell after implementing the tasks. It calls your functions in the required order and displays their results. This is a check of your work, not an extra task or additional marks. If a function is unfinished, return to that task. Function checks are independent: an unfinished earlier function does not prevent the grader checking later functions on its own inputs.\"]}, {\"cell_type\": \"code\", \"metadata\": {}, \"source\": [\"partitions = group_split(records)\\n\", \"training = [r for r in records if r[\\\"record_id\\\"] in partitions[\\\"train\\\"]]\\n\", \"validation = [r for r in records if r[\\\"record_id\\\"] in partitions[\\\"validation\\\"]]\\n\", \"features = [{k: v for k, v in r.items() if k != \\\"target\\\"} for r in validation]\\n\", \"predictions = predict_regression(training, features)\\n\", \"actual = [r[\\\"target\\\"] for r in validation]\\n\", \"for name, predicted in predictions.items():\\n\", \"    print(name, regression_errors(actual, predicted))\\n\", \"# E6 is reserved for final evaluation; do not use it to select a model.\\n\"], \"execution_count\": null, \"outputs\": []}, {\"cell_type\": \"markdown\", \"metadata\": {}, \"source\": [\"## Submit your test\\n\", \"Run the cell below and click **Submit test**. Open the generated form link, check your details and press **Submit** there